    "durationMs": 189045,
    "finalText": "Done. Both processes are zombies awaiting reap by init (parents died), and port 8000 is free — clean state.\n\nThe URL shortener is complete and fully tested. Here's what I built:\n\n**Structure**\n- `cmd/server/main.go` — reads `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials), runs migrations, serves on `0.0.0.0:8000`, graceful shutdown on SIGTERM\n- `internal/api/api.go` — chi v5.2.1 router with the four routes, validation, JSON responses\n- `internal/store/store.go` — persistence via `database/sql` + pgx (Go's idiomatic persistence layer)\n- `internal/migrate/` — embedded SQL migrations with a version-tracked runner (`schema_migrations` table), applied idempotently on startup\n- `start.sh` — executable; runs migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (binary pre-built, rebuilds if missing)\n- `README.md` — includes the \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Key behaviors verified by an end-to-end test suite against the live server**\n- POST returns `201 {code, url, clicks:0}`, echoing the submitted URL unchanged; generated codes are 8 random chars (with collision retry)\n- Duplicate custom code → `409`; malformed JSON, missing/invalid URL (`ftp://`, no scheme, empty host), and invalid codes (length, non-ASCII, bad chars) → `422` with `error` field\n- GET `/r/{code}` uses a single atomic `UPDATE ... clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url` — increments exactly once, 404 without touching counters\n- **Restart test passed**: killed and relaunched via `sh start.sh`; clicks (2→3) and all 5 links survived, migrations applied cleanly a second time, list order preserved\n\nDependencies are pinned (chi v5.2.1, pgx v5.7.6 — the newest pgx requires Go 1.25 which the toolchain can't fetch), and `gofmt`/`go vet` are clean."
